  "topicSummary": "IoT architecture, protocols (MQTT/HTTP), sensors, actuators, microcontrollers, firmware, cloud integration, case studies.",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "1. Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This module introduces IoT (Internet of Things) as the data acquisition layer in Urban Informatics."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Objective:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Understand how real-world data is collected",
        "Learn communication between devices and cloud",
        "Study hardware + software integration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "2. What is IoT?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> IoT refers to a network of physical devices that sense the environment, communicate data, and act automatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Examples in Cities:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Smart traffic lights",
        "Air quality sensors",
        "Smart parking systems"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "3. IoT Architecture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> IoT architecture defines how components interact from device to cloud."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Layers of IoT:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Layer", "Function"],
      "rows": [
        ["Perception Layer", "Sensors collect data"],
        ["Network Layer", "Transmit data"],
        ["Processing Layer", "Analyze data (cloud)"],
        ["Application Layer", "User interface"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Data Flow:</strong> Sensor → Microcontroller → Network → Cloud → Dashboard"
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "4. IoT Communication Protocols"
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "A. MQTT (Message Queuing Telemetry Transport)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Features:</strong> Lightweight, Publish/Subscribe model, Efficient for low bandwidth",
        "<strong>Publisher:</strong> sends data",
        "<strong>Broker:</strong> manages communication",
        "<strong>Subscriber:</strong> receives data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "B. HTTP (HyperText Transfer Protocol)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Request/Response model",
        "Widely used",
        "Higher overhead than MQTT"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "MQTT vs HTTP:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Feature", "MQTT", "HTTP"],
      "rows": [
        ["Model", "Publish/Subscribe", "Request/Response"],
        ["Efficiency", "High", "Moderate"],
        ["Use Case", "IoT devices", "Web services"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "5. Sensors"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Sensors are devices that collect data from the environment."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Types of Sensors:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Sensor", "Measures", "Urban Use"],
      "rows": [
        ["Temperature", "Heat", "Weather monitoring"],
        ["Gas", "Pollution", "Air quality"],
        ["Ultrasonic", "Distance", "Parking systems"],
        ["Camera", "Images", "Traffic monitoring"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "6. Actuators"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Actuators perform actions based on data received from sensors/controllers."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Examples:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Traffic light control",
        "Automatic gates",
        "Smart street lighting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Key Difference:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Sensor →</strong> collects data",
        "<strong>Actuator →</strong> performs action"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "7. Microcontrollers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Microcontrollers are small computing devices that control sensors and actuators."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Examples:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Arduino Uno",
        "ESP8266",
        "Raspberry Pi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Role:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Read sensor data",
        "Process signals",
        "Send data to cloud"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "8. Firmware"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Firmware is the software embedded in hardware devices that controls sensors, handles communication, and executes device logic."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Example:</strong> Code running on Arduino to read temperature and send data to the cloud."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Characteristics:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Low-level programming",
        "Real-time execution",
        "Controls sensors and actuators"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "9. Cloud Integration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Connecting IoT devices to cloud platforms for storage, processing, and visualization."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Platforms:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Amazon Web Services (AWS)",
        "Microsoft Azure",
        "Google Cloud"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Benefits:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Scalability",
        "Remote access",
        "Real-time analytics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "10. Case Studies (Urban Applications)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Smart Traffic System:</strong> Sensors detect vehicles → Microcontroller processes → Cloud optimizes signals.",
        "<strong>Air Quality Monitoring:</strong> Gas sensors measure pollution → Data sent to cloud → Dashboard displays AQI.",
        "<strong>Smart Parking:</strong> Ultrasonic sensors detect availability → Mobile app shows free slots.",
        "<strong>Smart Street Lighting:</strong> Motion sensors detect presence → Lights turn on/off automatically."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "11. IoT Workflow (Very Important)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "ordered",
      "items": [
        "Sensor collects data",
        "Microcontroller processes signals",
        "Data transmitted via MQTT/HTTP",
        "Cloud stores and analyzes",
        "Dashboard displays results",
        "Actuator performs action"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "examSummary": [
    "IoT = connected devices collecting and acting on data",
    "Architecture = Perception → Network → Processing → Application",
